package "mrta_mode (WS-driven position, REST as fallback only -- implemented)" #E8F5E9 {

    class GridStateManager <<REST client — bootstrap + fallback only>> {
        + base_url : str
        + cell_mm : int | None
        + map_cells_x, map_cells_y : int
        --
        + fetch_dotbots() : list[dict]        <GET /controller/dotbots>
        + fetch_map_size() : (int, int)       <GET /controller/map_size>
        + set_map_size(width_mm, height_mm) : void
        + mm_to_cell(x_mm, y_mm) : Coordinates2D
        + cell_to_mm(pos) : (float, float)
        + resolve_conflicts(positions) : dict[str, Coordinates2D]
    }
    note bottom of GridStateManager
      No longer the step-loop's position source.
      Used once at startup (map size + initial bot
      list) and by ControllerStatusListener as the
      degraded-mode fallback when the WS link is down
      -- same GET /controller/dotbots as before, just
      off the hot path. Position -> Coordinates2D rename
      only (from core import Position -> Coordinates2D);
      shape (frozen, hashable, .x/.y) is unchanged.
    end note

    class ControllerStatusListener <<new, replaces WaypointWatcher — WS client>> {
        + ws_url : str                         <ws://.../controller/ws/status>
        - _stop : Event
        --
        + start() : void
        + stop() : void
        - _listen_forever() : void
        - _handle_raw(raw) : void
        - _dispatch(notification) : void
    }
    note bottom of ControllerStatusListener
      Single WS connection, same endpoint as today.
      _dispatch() now reads *both* payload shapes carried
      by cmd=2 (UPDATE) instead of keeping one and
      dropping the other:
        - data.lh2_waypoints -> click_events queue
          (consumed by ManualClickTranslator, unchanged)
        - data.lh2_position   -> LivePositionStore.update()
          (new: was silently discarded before)
      Reconnect/backoff logic unchanged from WaypointWatcher.
    end note

    class LivePositionStore <<new>> {
        - _positions : dict[str, Coordinates2D]
        - _updated : dict[str, Event]
        --
        + update(address, position_mm) : void
        + snapshot() : dict[str, Coordinates2D]
        + wait_until_all_arrived(targets, timeout) : set[str]
    }
    note bottom of LivePositionStore
      Arrival is now event-driven: wait_until_all_arrived()
      blocks on per-bot Events set by update(), instead of
      DotBotNavigator's old GET /controller/dotbots poll loop.
      If no WS update arrives before `timeout`, falls back to
      one GridStateManager.fetch_dotbots() call -- same safety
      net principle as ManualClickTranslator.reconcile().
    end note

    class ManualClickTranslator <<unchanged shape, Position -> Coordinates2D>> {
        - _commanded : dict[str, Coordinates2D]
        --
        + seed_commanded(dotbots_raw) : void
        + record_commanded(address, cell) : void
        + translate(waypoints_mm, current) : list[Coordinates2D]
        + is_self_commanded(event) : bool
        + reconcile() : list[ClickEvent]         <-- REST fallback,
                                                       GridStateManager.fetch_dotbots()
    }

    class WaypointCommandClient <<renamed from DotBotNavigator — write-path only>> {
        + base_url : str
        + threshold : int
        --
        + send(address, waypoints_mm) : void          <PUT /controller/dotbots/{address}/0/waypoints>
        + send_all_parallel(moved_mm) : void           <N parallel PUTs, same route>
    }
    note bottom of WaypointCommandClient
      Arrival-waiting method removed: that responsibility
      moved to LivePositionStore, which already has the
      live data. This class purely issues commands.
    end note

    class MRTASession <<the "activatable mode" object>> {
        + engine : WorldEngine
        + agents : list[Agent]
        - _orchestrator : LifelongGoalOrchestrator
        - _active_target : dict[int, Coordinates2D | None]
        - _pending_chain : dict[int, deque[Coordinates2D]]
        --
        + start() : void
        + stop() : void
        + handle_click(event: ClickEvent) : void
        + tick() : void
        - _advance_chain(agent_id) : void
    }
    note bottom of MRTASession
      tick() calls LivePositionStore.wait_until_all_arrived(),
      event-driven instead of polling -- unchanged from before
      this reconnection.

      **handle_click() -- settled, no longer open.** Translates the
      waypoint chain to cells via ManualClickTranslator (unchanged).
      Empty chain (Stop-nav, or nothing to do) -> cancel: calls
      _orchestrator.set_target(agent_id, agent.position) so
      assign_missions() clears the slot next tick (position == target),
      and drops any queued chain. Non-empty chain -> calls
      _orchestrator.set_target(agent_id, cells[0]) (overwrites any
      in-flight target unconditionally -- LifelongGoalOrchestrator's
      own contract, so a re-click needs no separate cancel step) and
      stores cells[1:] in _pending_chain[agent_id].

      **Multi-hop waypoint chains -- new, MRTASession's own job.**
      LifelongGoalOrchestrator holds exactly one mutable target slot
      per agent, no queue (unlike the old FleetManager/Task model,
      where each chain cell became its own queued Task). So the chain
      is now owned locally: after each advance_time_step(), for every
      agent whose position == _active_target[agent_id] and whose
      _pending_chain[agent_id] is non-empty, _advance_chain() pops the
      next cell and calls set_target() again. _active_target mirrors
      the orchestrator's private _target dict (read-only, kept in sync
      by MRTASession itself since it is the only caller of
      set_target()) -- used both for this and to replace the old
      "if not self.fleet.tasks: sleep(idle)" idle check (now:
      "if not any(_active_target.values()) and not events: sleep").

      **Cancel-on-empty-waypoint (Button.md fix C.3) -- same
      mechanism as the rest of cancel**, not a separate code path:
      set_target(agent_id, agent.position) either way.
    end note

    class MRTACli <<kept, thinned>> {
        --
        + main() : void
    }
}

package "MAPF_Simulation (external repo, pip-installed -- core + pibt)" #EAF4FF {
    class WorldEngine
    class Grid2D
    class Agent
    class Objective
    class AssignmentManifest
    class StepOutcome
    class PathPlanner <<interface>>
    class MissionOrchestrator <<interface>>
    class PIBTPlanner
    class LifelongGoalOrchestrator
    PathPlanner <|.. PIBTPlanner
    MissionOrchestrator <|.. LifelongGoalOrchestrator
    WorldEngine *-- PathPlanner
