}
note bottom of PathPlanner
  Replaces the vendored simulation/ copy this diagram used to show as
  "unchanged": that copy is retired (dotbot-logistics commit d4e053b).
  Imported instead from the pip-installed `mapf-simulation` package
  (pyproject.toml on ~/3A/projets/MAPF_Simulation's develop branch,
  git@github.com:RasdaCorentin/MAPF_Simulation, `include = ["core*",
  "pibt*"]`) -- top-level `import core` / `import pibt`, no sys.path
  insert needed once installed. No FleetManager, QueueTaskSource, Task,
  Allocator or PIBTCoordinator survive on the other side of this import:
  `core.Agent`/`core.Grid2D`/`core.WorldEngine` replace
  `Agent`/`Grid`/`Simulation`; `pibt.PIBTPlanner` replaces
  `PIBTCoordinator`; `core.Coordinates2D` replaces `Position`.
end note
note bottom of LifelongGoalOrchestrator
  **The actual replacement for the allocation layer -- confirmed,
  imported as-is, nothing reimplemented upstream.** One mutable target
  slot per agent (`_target: dict[int, Coordinates2D | None]`), written
  only through set_target(agent_id, position) -- no shared pool, no
  arbitration between agents, because there is nothing to arbitrate:
  the caller that owns the goal source decides per agent. Per its own
  docstring, this class was written *for this exact use case*
  ("an operator click translated by sim_dotbot_mrta.py's
  ManualClickTranslator, the use case this class actually serves").

  The two scope cuts the pre-32dfe2f draft of this note worried about
  are both resolved by set_target()'s shape, not by anything MRTASession
  still has to build:
  1. **Eligibility** -- moot. A click already means "this one bot" by
     construction: set_target() takes an explicit agent_id, there is no
     pool to draw the wrong agent from.
  2. **Idle/parked state** -- built in. assign_missions() clears an
     agent's slot to None the instant position == target and omits it
     from goals; it stays parked until set_target() is called again.
     Matches MRTA's "every bot starts parked" invariant exactly, no
     workaround needed.

  Requires PIBTPlanner's GoalReachedPolicy.TRANSIENT (its default): an
  agent demoted to -inf priority on arrival must be undemoted the
  instant it is re-targeted. What is NOT built in, and is MRTASession's
  job (see its note): multi-hop waypoint chains (one slot, no queue)
  and preventing two agents being set to the same target -- both
  explicitly left to the caller per pibt/AGENT.md.
end note

MRTASession *-- GridStateManager
MRTASession *-- ControllerStatusListener
MRTASession *-- LivePositionStore
MRTASession *-- ManualClickTranslator
MRTASession *-- WaypointCommandClient
MRTASession *-- WorldEngine
MRTASession *-- LifelongGoalOrchestrator
MRTASession o-- Agent

ControllerStatusListener ..> ManualClickTranslator : click events\n(data.lh2_waypoints)
ControllerStatusListener ..> LivePositionStore : position events\n(data.lh2_position)

ManualClickTranslator ..> GridStateManager : uses (mm_to_cell,\nREST fallback)
LivePositionStore ..> GridStateManager : REST fallback only\n(WS outage)
WaypointCommandClient ..> GridStateManager : uses (cell_to_mm)

MRTACli ..> MRTASession : builds & runs (CLI driver)

@enduml
